        "title": "Semiotics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Semiotics is the study of signs and sign systems — how meaning is produced, transmitted, and interpreted. It is broader than linguistics: any systematic process of meaning-making is semiotic. This includes visual design, architecture, film, music, ritual, and — crucially — programming languages, APIs, and user interfaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiotics:00-overview, git-history:semiotics:00-overview]",
