      "text": "## Denotation / Connotation / Myth (Barthes' Layers)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#025",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiotics:00-overview, git-history:semiotics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiotics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "semiotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Semiotics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  FIRST ORDER — DENOTATION\n  +---------------------------+\n  |  Signifier  |  Signified  |\n  +---------------------------+\n  Examples: \"rose\" (word) → rose (flower)\n            Photo of steak → steak (food)\n           |\n           | whole first-order sign becomes a new Signifier\n           v\n  SECOND ORDER — CONNOTATION / MYTH\n  +---------------------------+\n  |  Sign₁     |  New         |\n  |  (first    |  Signified   |\n  |  order)    |  (cultural,  |\n  |            |  ideological)|\n  +---------------------------+\n  Examples: rose → ROMANCE / PASSION\n            steak → FRENCHNESS (Barthes)\n            white coat → MEDICAL AUTHORITY\n            cowboy → AMERICAN FREEDOM"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#026",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiotics:00-overview, git-history:semiotics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiotics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "semiotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Semiotics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MYTH (Barthes): operates at second order.\n  Takes historically contingent connotations and\n  presents them as NATURAL and INEVITABLE.\n  \"This is just how things are.\"\n  = ideology rendering contingency as necessity.\n```"
    },
