      "text": "## Jakobson's Six Functions of Language"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#032",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiotics:00-overview, git-history:semiotics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiotics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "semiotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Semiotics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Essential framework: every communicative act orients toward one of six factors, activating a different function."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#033",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:semiotics:00-overview, git-history:semiotics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "semiotics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiotics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "semiotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Semiotics - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  +---------------------+\n  |      CONTEXT        |\n  |  (what the message  |\n  |    is about)        |\n  +---------------------+\n  REFERENTIAL function: pointing to the world; informational\n           |\n  SENDER ——————→ MESSAGE ——————→ RECEIVER\n  (EMOTIVE      (POETIC          (CONATIVE\n  function:     function:        function:\n  expresses     focused on       oriented\n  speaker's     form of          toward\n  state)        message itself)  addressee;\n                                 commands,\n                                 appeals)\n           |\n  +---------------------+\n  |       CONTACT       |\n  |   (channel/medium)  |\n  +---------------------+\n  PHATIC function: maintaining contact (\"Hello?\", \"You know what I mean?\")"
    },
